			(property "Description" "Raspberry Pi RP2040 MCU\n\n56-pin 32-bit Microcontroller with 264kB of SRAM and external flash support up to 16MB\n\nhttps://pico.raspberrypi.org/getting-started/ Getting Started with the RP2040\n\n• Dual-core ARM Cortex M0+ processor, flexible clock running up to 133 MHz\n•\n• 264kB of SRAM, and QSPI control of common flash memory\n•\n• USB 1.1 Host and Device support\n•\n• Low-power sleep and dormant modes\n•\n• Drag & drop programming using mass storage over USB\n•\n• 26 multi-function GPIO pins\n•\n• 2×SPI, 2×I2C, 2×UART, 3×12-bit ADC, 16×controllable PWM channels\n•\n• Accurate clock and timer on-chip\n•\n• Temperature sensor\n•\n• Accelerated floating point libraries on-chip\n•\n• 8×Programmable IO (PIO) state machines for custom peripheral support\n•"
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
